# Daintree Assistant Server — example environment configuration.
# Copy to .env for local development. NEVER commit real secret values.

# --- Environment ---
ENVIRONMENT=development
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Set DAINTREE_LOG_CONSOLE=1 for human-readable logs in a terminal.

# Bind address for `python -m daintree_assistant_server`. Cloud Run injects
# PORT=8080; pick a fixed local dev port your CLI can always target.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8473

# --- Upstream provider (OpenRouter; OpenAI-compatible) ---
# Models are hardcoded (a product decision; see config.py): the main completion,
# the selector, the utility tasks, and the skill-learning gate all use
# deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731, reached through OpenRouter rather than the
# DeepSeek API directly. (The skill builder/improver name a stronger model,
# openai/gpt-5.6-sol, over this same key — see the skill-learning section below.)
# So is the endpoint-selection policy:
# OpenRouter fronts ~24 endpoints serving these weights, and every request pins
# sort=throughput (fastest tokens/sec wins, price second) filtered to
# data_collection=deny — endpoints that do not COLLECT prompt data or train on
# it. That is a no-training guarantee, NOT a no-retention one: zero data
# retention is OpenRouter's separate `zdr` flag, which this server does not send
# by default. See docs/PROVIDER_POLICY.md and _PROVIDER_ROUTING in
# providers/openrouter.py. Only the key and base URL are configurable.
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# BENCHMARK / LIVE-TEST TOOLING ONLY. The server itself holds NO upstream
# credential: every request's bearer token IS the OpenRouter key that funds its
# upstream calls (see auth.py), and the serving path never reads this variable.
# Set it to run benchmarks/ or RUN_LIVE_OPENROUTER=1 tests.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Retained but UNUSED — nothing reads it now that the upstream is OpenRouter.
# Kept so switching back to the direct DeepSeek API is a code change, not a key
# hunt.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# --- Thinking ---
# The thinking POSTURE is hardcoded, not configurable (a product decision, like
# the model ids). THE WHOLE INTERACTIVE SURFACE IS NON-THINKING: the main
# completion, every utility task, and the skill selector all send reasoning
# explicitly disabled (INTERACTIVE_THINKING_ENABLED = False in config.py). The
# selector keeps a second, independent hardcode of its own so re-enabling the
# interactive posture cannot drag it along; its prompt's reason-first JSON key
# order supplies the inline reasoning instead.
# The only surface that still thinks is SKILL LEARNING — the gate (thinking-high
# on the small model) and the builder/improver (high effort on GPT-5.6 Sol).
# It runs fire-and-forget after the response, so its latency never reaches a user.
# Because max_tokens is shared by reasoning + output, those small-output thinking
# calls add this many tokens of headroom to their caps:
THINKING_HEADROOM_TOKENS=4000

# --- Authentication ---
# There is no server-side API key. Every request carries the caller's own key
# as its bearer token (for early testers, their OpenRouter key); a request
# without one is rejected in every environment, and that same key funds the
# turn's upstream calls.

# --- State signing (HMAC; distinct from the callers' API keys) ---
STATE_SIGNING_KEY_CURRENT=replace-me-with-32+-random-bytes
STATE_SIGNING_KID=state-2026-06
# Optional previous key for zero-downtime rotation:
# STATE_SIGNING_KEY_PREVIOUS=...
# STATE_SIGNING_KID_PREVIOUS=state-2026-05
STATE_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS=604800
STATE_SALT=replace-me

# --- Limits ---
MAX_REQUEST_BYTES=8388608
MAX_TOOLS=128
MAX_ACTIVE_SKILLS=3

# --- Timeouts (seconds) ---
# The selector timeout is a first-byte latency budget (a transient failure gets
# ONE retry); non-thinking selector calls run 1.2-2.6s, so 8s is already generous.
SELECTOR_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=8
MAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=840
# Default budget for the small utility tasks (classify, judge, summarize,
# extract). The heavyweight transcript/graph tasks (checkpoint, memory_distill,
# workflow_*) carry their own explicit 60s budget on their TaskProfile.
UTILITY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60

# --- Retries ---
# THIS SETTING GOVERNS ONE HOP ONLY: backend → OpenRouter. Every upstream call
# (main completion, stream open, selector, utility tasks) retries transient
# failures (5xx, timeouts, rate limits, transport errors). On the non-streaming
# path this happens before any public bytes; a STREAMING turn may still retry the
# open/prefetch after the `meta` event has been emitted, but never once a model
# delta has been sent. The normal posture is ONE retry (up to 2 attempts).
#
# THERE IS A SECOND, LEGITIMATE RETRY LAYER on the OTHER hop: CLI → backend
# (cli/internal/backend/retry.go — up to 10 attempts inside a 2-minute window,
# sized to ride out a backend restart). These are different networks and
# different failure modes, so they coexist by design; the CLI does not replay a
# deterministic failure or a turn that has already streamed visible tokens. See
# docs/PROVIDER_POLICY.md for how the two layers compose.
#
# Each attempt gets the full per-call timeout above. Note what that timeout IS: an
# httpx READ budget — the maximum gap between chunks — not a total wall clock, with
# connect/write/pool bounded separately. So "(1 + retries) x timeout" is a rough
# worst case for a fully stalled upstream, NOT a ceiling on turn duration: a
# response that keeps trickling bytes resets the read clock indefinitely. A real
# end-to-end deadline is separate work.
# A valid upstream Retry-After is AUTHORITATIVE and replaces the computed backoff
# entirely (including 0, i.e. retry at once). One LARGER than 10s abandons the
# retry instead of waiting — a live turn cannot absorb that pause.
MAX_UPSTREAM_RETRIES=1
# Exponential backoff base. The wait is base * 2**attempt, capped at 5s, PLUS up
# to one extra `base` of jitter — so the real ceiling is 5s + base (5.25s at the
# default). Set to 0 to retry immediately with no backoff.
RETRY_BACKOFF_BASE_SECONDS=0.25


# --- Policy ---
ALLOW_REMOTE_IMAGE_URLS=false
EXPOSE_DEBUG_SELECTOR_REASON=false

# --- Skill learning (LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY) ---
# A backend-internal harness that watches completed local workflows and writes or
# improves skill files so the catalog "learns". Entirely invisible to the CLI: no
# new wire fields, and the main assistant model is never told it exists — a created
# skill simply appears as a normal dynamic skill load. MUST be off in production:
# an enabled mode fails /readyz there. Leave OFF unless you are iterating on skills.
#   off     — disabled (default)
#   propose — run the gate (small model) + the openai/gpt-5.6-sol builder/improver
#             and write a proposal + audit JSON under SKILL_LEARNING_AUDIT_DIR, but
#             never touch skill files
#   apply   — also write/rewrite the skill file and reload the catalog in place
SKILL_LEARNING_MODE=off
# Where created/improved skills are written. Empty → the packaged skills dir
# (edit-in-place; improvements show up in `git diff`, ready to commit). Set to a
# separate dir (e.g. .daintree/skills) to keep the source tree untouched — the
# catalog then loads packaged skills PLUS that overlay.
SKILL_LEARNING_DIR=
# Per-change audit + proposal JSON records land here (gitignored).
SKILL_LEARNING_AUDIT_DIR=.daintree/skill-learning
# Gate verdicts below this confidence never write.
SKILL_LEARNING_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.75
# Minimum conversation messages before learning is considered (needs prior work).
SKILL_LEARNING_MIN_MESSAGES=3
# Allow the learner to MINT a new foundation skill or PROMOTE a specific one to
# foundation. Off by default (a foundation is near-always-loaded, so tiering one is a
# human curation decision); the learner can always IMPROVE an existing foundation.
SKILL_LEARNING_ALLOW_FOUNDATION_CREATE=false

# --- Upstream request dumping (LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY) ---
# When set, every upstream request body is written there as numbered
# pretty-printed JSON — the prompt-cache forensics tool (diff two dumps to find
# the byte where "identical" requests diverge). Contains FULL prompts; a set
# value in production fails /readyz.
# DAINTREE_DUMP_UPSTREAM_DIR=

